Fork divergence of the vendored MAYO-C subtree from upstream
PQCMayo/MAYO-C @ 4b7cd94c96b9522864efe40c6ad1fa269584a807.

Exactly one file differs across the compiled src/ + include/ subtree
(39 of 40 files byte-identical). Rationale: see ../MAYO-PROVENANCE.md (T2.1-c).
The upstream header declared shake256 as `int`, but fips202.c *defines* it as
`void` (lines 134/890, identical in both trees) — a stale forward declaration.
wasm-ld links the type mismatch with only a warning and the call traps at
runtime; correcting the declaration fixes the build. Function body untouched.

--- upstream  src/common/fips202.h
+++ vendored  src/common/fips202.h
@@ -6,7 +6,7 @@
 #include <stddef.h>
 
 int shake128(unsigned char *output, size_t outputByteLen, const unsigned char *input, size_t inputByteLen);
-int shake256(unsigned char *output, size_t outputByteLen, const unsigned char *input, size_t inputByteLen);
+void shake256(unsigned char *output, size_t outputByteLen, const unsigned char *input, size_t inputByteLen);
 
 #endif
